  "coach": "Claudio Ranieri",
  "team": "Leicester City 2015-16",
  "system": "Compact 4-4-2 block + the league's fastest transition (Kante wins it, Vardy runs behind)",
  "name": "The 5000-1",
  "keyPrinciple": "Simplicity executed perfectly beats complexity executed imperfectly — do the simple things without error, every match.",
  "smUnits": [
   "Coaching point: Simplicity executed perfectly beats complexity executed imperfectly — do the simple things without error, every match.",
   "WHY LEICESTER 2016 IS IMPORTANT",
   "THE SQUAD — HOW IT WAS BUILT"
  ],
  "description": "Leicester started the 2015-16 season at 5000-1 — a squad of players the market undervalued (Vardy from non-league, Mahrez for around 400k, Kante for under 6m) organized into a compact 4-4-2 block with the Premier League's fastest transition: Kante breaking up play and distributing instantly while Vardy was already running behind the line. Ranieri's contribution was psychological — trust, calm and joy (pizza after clean sheets) while England waited for the collapse that never came. No moment of invention decided the season; a simple thing executed without error forty-six times did.",
